            <ArticleTitle>Video-assisted thoracoscopic surgery lobectomy for lung cancer.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>27-38, v</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.soc.2012.09.001</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1055-3207(12)00086-5</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Surgical resection is currently the gold standard in operable patients with early-stage lung cancer. Video-assisted thoracoscopic surgery (VATS) lobectomy is a technique that has technically evolved and grown increasingly popular over the past two decades. This article presents the evolution, definition, current application, and some of the controversies surrounding VATS lobectomy.</AbstractText>
